e="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item><item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item></items><chunks count="1"><chunk name="Container"><items count="8"><item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item><item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">a9fd121c-5187-430a-9e38-3f1654d40b33</item><item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item><item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10"></item><item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item><item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item><item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item><item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">HERO · TURNING BRICKS ON RODS · آجرهای چرخان روی میله
Open hero-rod-facade-context.3dm first (the house behind). Units: metres.

Every brick has one hole and turns on a vertical steel rod. The picture (a grey image, 0.5 = straight)
turns each brick up to 80° one way or the other; the brick ends are glazed (lapis one end, turquoise the other),
so a turn + shows turquoise and a turn − shows lapis: from the street the waves appear in colour.
Side gap 30 mm ≥ brick diagonal − length (224 − 200): any turn of any neighbour is collision-free.
Site: Raj sheet = turn and coloured end of every brick, rod by rod; Stencils = one angle template per turn.

Idea after Iranian turning-brick façades on rods; picture and building are our own study.</item></items><chunks count="2"><chunk name="Attributes"><items count="5"><item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35"><X>40</X><Y>20</Y><W>760</W><H>190</H></item><item name="MarginLeft" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item><item name="MarginRight" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item><item name="MarginTop" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item><item name="Pivot" type_name="gh_drawing_pointf" type_code="31"><X>420.0</X><Y>115.0</Y></item></items></chunk><chunk name="PanelProperties"><items count="7"><item name="Colour" type_name="gh_drawing_color" type_code="36"><ARGB>255;255;250;90</ARGB></item><item name="DrawIndices" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item><item name="DrawPaths" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item><item name="Multiline" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item><item name="SpecialCodes" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item><item name="Stream" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item><item name="Wrap" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item></items></chunk></chunks></chunk></chunks></chunk><chunk name="Object" index="1"><items count="2"><item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">fbac3e32-f100-4292-8692-77240a42fd1a</item><item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Point</item></items><chunks count="1"><chunk name="Container"><items count="6"><item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Contains a collection of three-dimensional points</item><item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">0eb28a0a-67cc-4e7c-b727-b4fe2083b91a</item><item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Point</item><item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Pt</item><item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item><item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item></items><chunks count="2"><chunk name="